    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Fever, sore throat and cough for two days; home COVID-19 test positive. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Aurelius called this morning after a positive home antigen test and was seen the same day at the end of clinic, masked and in a separate room. Two days ago he developed a sore throat, aches and a temperature of 38.5 °C, followed by a dry cough. Several people on his staff have been unwell this week. He is not short of breath, has no chest pain, and can walk about his quarters without difficulty. He is eating little but drinking well. He had his last COVID-19 vaccine about ten months ago. His reflux has been quiet on omeprazole. He has taken his herbal paste as usual on alternate nights, no more, and asks whether he may take a cough syrup at night to sleep. The repeat antigen test here is positive. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Two days ago, after contacts at work were unwell</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Fever to 38.5 °C, sore throat, dry cough, aches; no breathlessness or chest pain</td></tr><tr><td>Test</td><td>Rapid SARS-CoV-2 antigen test positive at home and in clinic</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Age 53; vaccinated about ten months ago; no lung, heart, kidney or immune condition; opium-containing remedy on alternate nights; omeprazole</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
