    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Burning and pressing pain in the upper abdomen and lower chest after meals, for more than a year and worse over three months, with poor appetite, waking at night with pain and a sour taste, and a 3 kg weight loss; not brought on by exertion; normal ECG; cardiac and peptic causes to be excluded</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R10.13</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting concern at the index visit, superseded by the diagnosis at endoscopy; its pattern echoes the stomach and chest complaints and the pain with food that Dio describes (D).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Gastroesophageal reflux disease with erosive esophagitis, Los Angeles grade B, and a 2 cm sliding hiatal hernia; Helicobacter pylori negative on biopsy; coronary disease excluded by CT coronary angiography; synthetic modern diagnosis for his documented stomach and chest complaints</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>K21.00</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis; the cause of his real complaints is unknown and no historical diagnosis is made.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Daily use of an unregulated opium-containing herbal remedy for about six years, for stomach pain and sleep; opioid use disorder criteria not met (one DSM-5-TR criterion, restlessness and poor sleep when he stopped it); expected physiological dependence; constipation and possibly slowed gastric emptying from the opioid</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F11.90</td><td>S — Synthetic modern finding anchored to the theriac he took (D); no opioid use disorder or addiction is attributed to him (the claim is disputed, R).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Chronic insomnia disorder for more than a year, with waking from night pain and trouble returning to sleep; Insomnia Severity Index 17 (moderate)</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>G47.00</td><td>S — Synthetic modern finding anchored to Galen&apos;s account of his sleeplessness without the poppy juice (D, possible).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Sustained strain of command: leads a large organization through a long field assignment far from home, with long days and little rest</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z56.6</td><td>S — Synthetic work strain anchored to his documented years on campaign (D).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-6">
    <td>Constipation from the opioid in his remedy: hard stools every two or three days</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>K59.03</td><td>S — Synthetic finding at intake.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-7">
    <td>COVID-19, mild (rapid antigen test positive), without breathlessness or low oxygen; antiviral treatment offered and declined; resolved</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>U07.1</td><td>S — Synthetic intercurrent illness; not a claim about the Antonine Plague or about any illness in his lifetime.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

